 future knockouts rather than isolated damage."]},{"id":"339","title":"Basic Box","publishedAt":"2026-09-27","sourceUrls":["https://limitlesstcg.com/decks/339","https://www.tcgdex.net/database/me/me01/104","https://www.tcgdex.net/database/sv/sv06/025"],"signatureCards":["me01-104","sv06-025"],"gamePlan":"Use a selection of Basic attackers for different board states. Mega Kangaskhan ex supplies Active-position draw, while Teal Mask Ogerpon ex supports a Grass Energy engine.","strengths":["Basic attackers reduce evolution setup requirements.","Several attackers allow different tactical routes."],"weaknesses":["Multiple Energy requirements compete for deck space.","Rule Box attackers expose multiple Prizes when knocked out."],"suggestions":["Keep Energy access aligned with the attackers you actually plan to use.","Review opening Pokémon and switching options alongside the draw engine."]},{"id":"322","title":"Slowking","publishedAt":"2026-09-27","sourceUrls":["https://limitlesstcg.com/decks/322","https://www.tcgdex.net/database/sv/sv07/058"],"signatureCards":["sv07-058"],"gamePlan":"Seek Inspiration copies an attack from a discarded non-Rule-Box Pokémon on top of the deck. Build around controlling that top card and matching copied attacks to the situation.","strengths":["Access to different non-Rule-Box attacks.","A single-Prize main attacker can support flexible exchanges."],"weaknesses":["An unsuitable top card can make the attack fail.","Requires both evolution setup and reliable top-deck control."],"suggestions":["Check each chosen attack donor against Seek Inspiration restrictions.","Include a plan for recovering discarded attackers and resetting the deck top."]},{"id":"350?variant=1","title":"Alakazam Dudunsparce","publishedAt":"2026-09-27","sourceUrls":["https://limitlesstcg.com/decks/350?variant=1","https://www.tcgdex.net/database/me/me01/056","https://www.tcgdex.net/database/sv/sv05/129"],"signatureCards":["me01-056","sv05-129"],"gamePlan":"Grow the hand with Psychic Draw and Run Away Draw, then use Powerful Hand to place damage counters according to hand size.","strengths":["Powerful Hand scales with cards held in hand.","Dudunsparce recycles itself while drawing."],"weaknesses":["Hand disruption reduces the attack ceiling.","Several evolution lines can compete for setup resources."],"suggestions":["Preserve hand resources before committing to Powerful Hand.","Balance the Alakazam and Dudunsparce lines with recovery and search."]},{"id":"284?variant=3","title":"Dragapult Dusknoir","publishedAt":"2026-09-27","sourceUrls":["https://limitlesstcg.com/decks/284?variant=3","https://www.tcgdex.net/database/sv/sv06/130","https://www.tcgdex.net/database/sv/sv08.5/037"],"signatureCards":["sv06-130","sv08.5-037"],"gamePlan":"Combine Phantom Dive spread with Dusknoir’s Cursed Blast to reach knockout thresholds. Cursed Blast also knocks out your own Dusknoir, so map both sides of the Prize exchange.","strengths":["Additional targeted damage counters can finish difficult targets.","Several simultaneous knockout routes can emerge."],"weaknesses":["Cursed Blast gives up a Pokémon and potentially a Prize.","A second Stage 2 line increases setup demands."],"suggestions":["Count Prizes before using Cursed Blast.","Preserve enough resources to rebuild the main attacker after a knockout."]},{"id":"284?variant=9","title":"Dragapult Blaziken","publishedAt":"2026-09-27","sourceUrls":["https://limitlesstcg.com/decks/284?variant=9","https://www.tcgdex.net/database/sv/sv06/130","https://www.tcgdex.net/database/sv/sv09/024"],"signatureCards":["sv06-130","sv09-024"],"gamePlan":"Use Blaziken ex’s Seething Spirit to recover Basic Energy from the discard and support Dragapult’s multi-type attack cost.","strengths":["Recurring Energy attachment supports rebuilding attackers.","Blaziken can serve as an alternate attacking route."],"weaknesses":["Two Stage 2 lines need space and setup time.","Energy recovery depends on Energy reaching the discard."],"suggestions":["Map the evolution counts for both lines.","Keep Basic Energy and discard access consistent with Seething Spirit."]},{"id":"284?variant=12","title":"Dragapult Dudunsparce","publishedAt":"2026-09-27","sourceUrls":["https://limitlesstcg.com/decks/284?variant=12","https://www.tcgdex.net/database/sv/sv06/130","https://www.tcgdex.net/database/sv/sv05/129"],"signatureCards":["sv06-130","sv05-129"],"gamePlan":"Support Dragapult’s spread plan with Run Away Draw. Recycling Dudunsparce changes Bench space and requires rebuilding its line on later turns.","strengths":["A renewable draw option supports the Stage 2 setup.","Returning Dudunsparce can free Bench space."],"weaknesses":["Both lines need repeated evolution access.","Draw does not by itself guarantee the right Energy mix."],"suggestions":["Check the Dunsparce count against repeated Run Away Draw uses.","Keep a separate plan for finding Fire and Psychic Energy."]},{"id":"352","title":"Hydrapple","publishedAt":"2026-09-27","sourceUrls":["https://limitlesstcg.com/decks/352","https://www.tcgdex.net/database/sv/sv07/014","https://www.tcgdex.net/database/sv/sv06/025"],"signatureCards":["sv07-014","sv06-025"],"gamePlan":"Attach Grass Energy through Ripening Charge and the Ogerpon engine, then scale Syrup Storm with Energy across your board.","strengths":["Energy attachments increase offensive pressure.","Ripening Charge also heals the receiving Pokémon."],"weaknesses":["A large Energy board is a resource commitment.","Hydrapple is a Stage 2 attacker requiring evolution access."],"suggestions":["Balance Basic Grass Energy with reliable search/recovery.","Consider how to rebuild Energy attachments after a knockout."]},{"id":"320","title":"N's Zoroark","publishedAt":"2026-09-27","sourceUrls":["https://limitlesstcg.com/decks/320","https://www.tcgdex.net/database/sv/sv09/098"],"signatureCards":["sv09-098"],"gamePlan":"Use Trade to cycle the hand and Night Joker to copy attacks from Benched N’s Pokémon.","strengths":["Trade provides repeated card access.","Night Joker offers several attacks through the Bench."],"weaknesses":["Attack choices depend on specific Benched Pokémon.","Trade costs a discard that may remove future resources."],"suggestions":["Choose attack donors deliberately.","Review Bench space, Darkness Energy access and recovery together."]}]}